Dr.Jit is a just-in-time (JIT) compiler for ordinary and differentiable
computation. It traces Python or C++ array programs, fuses them into
kernels and compiles them for the CPU (via LLVM) or for the GPU (CUDA,
or Metal on Apple Silicon). Its automatic differentiation layer is the
foundation of the Mitsuba 3 differentiable renderer.

This package provides the Python module, the drjit-core JIT library
(LLVM backend, plus the Metal backend on macOS) and the C++ headers.
